[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186164197 :answer-field/choices 17592186164198] [:db/retract 17592186164197 :answer-field/choices 17592186164199] [:db/retract 17592186164197 :answer-field/choices 17592186164200] [:db/retract 17592186164197 :answer-field/choices 17592186164201] [:db/retract 17592186164197 :answer-field/choices 17592186164202] {:db/id 17592186167196 :question/worked-solution "Writing a decoupled system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {\\lambda }_{2}\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvectors are parallel to the axes. These correspond to so-called straight-line solutions of the form\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, notice that:\n\n- The tangents along the $x$-axis are pointing away from the origin, meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{1}>0.$\n\n- The tangents along the $y$-axis are pointing toward the origin, meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{2}<0.$\n\nAmong the options, the only system that satisfies ${\\lambda }_{1}>0$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}<0$ is the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-3y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164197 :answer-field/correct "answer-046949a3-90df-516c-995b-b46249819ead" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4a051744-2fdf-5555-a542-727518fba033" "answer-4dde6904-218e-5e1b-bfed-644cb9dc6af4" "answer-f19495bb-f541-5c6f-9b64-66ca79e589a2" "answer-046949a3-90df-516c-995b-b46249819ead" "answer-3b8c1fd7-4dd8-502c-b528-815a2db63d69"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a051744-2fdf-5555-a542-727518fba033" :answer/id #uuid "4a051744-2fdf-5555-a542-727518fba033" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-2x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-3y(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4dde6904-218e-5e1b-bfed-644cb9dc6af4" :answer/id #uuid "4dde6904-218e-5e1b-bfed-644cb9dc6af4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-2x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=3y(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f19495bb-f541-5c6f-9b64-66ca79e589a2" :answer/id #uuid "f19495bb-f541-5c6f-9b64-66ca79e589a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-3x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-2y(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-046949a3-90df-516c-995b-b46249819ead" :answer/id #uuid "046949a3-90df-516c-995b-b46249819ead" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-3y(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b8c1fd7-4dd8-502c-b528-815a2db63d69" :answer/id #uuid "3b8c1fd7-4dd8-502c-b528-815a2db63d69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=3y(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-9758d25e-c814-56ab-8f11-e4e0bcfceb89" :activity/id #uuid "9758d25e-c814-56ab-8f11-e4e0bcfceb89" :activity/title "Phase Portraits for Decoupled Linear Systems" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048395 :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-5a520d7a-4290-5de8-b947-6a2f2d894da8" "step-1ef10e0f-96f2-5d92-bbe2-eefc5b7495e0" "step-d8da57ac-8746-5f2f-9343-2e578146a3ec" "step-d2c62563-705f-59fb-a9e5-3dccacb8c397" "step-7d0a1590-0ec1-5f49-a23a-1c7464794346"] :activity/fi